00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:55,140
Please forgive us.

272
00:13:55,280 --> 00:13:55,740
Oh, no.

273
00:13:55,920 --> 00:13:57,420
It's really not that big a deal to me.

274
00:13:59,460 --> 00:14:00,160
Look at them!

275
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:02,360
They're so super alike, it's crazy!

276
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:03,960
That's no surprise.

277
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,840
We are related, after all.

278
00:14:06,060 --> 00:14:07,760
Yeah, it's funny you should mention that.

279
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:10,260
I've been his little sister for as long as I can remember.

280
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:12,400
Wow, what a coincidence.

281
00:14:12,780 --> 00:14:14,060
Does that make you my big sister?

282
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:15,120
No, of course not!

283
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:19,620
We were both still little kids when my family adopted Shido, so we're as close to siblings

284
00:14:19,620 --> 00:14:20,380
as we can be.

285
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:22,600
You mean, except for actually being siblings.

286
00:14:22,700 --> 00:14:25,640
Hey, Mana, little sis, I've got a question for you.

287
00:14:25,660 --> 00:14:25,840
Oh?

288
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:27,600
Go ahead and ask away, then.

289
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:27,980
Huh.

290
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:30,120
Well, uh, it's just that...

291
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:33,520
Well, no offense, but, uh, I don't remember you.

292
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:35,020
That doesn't surprise me.

293
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:36,160
It's weird.

294
00:14:36,420 --> 00:14:39,340
The past is such a blank that sometimes I think my memory's been erased.

295
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:39,800
Huh?

296
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:39,980
Huh?

297
00:14:39,980 --> 00:14:41,620
You've gotta be kidding me!

298
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:43,860
What the heck do you mean your memory's been erased?

299
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:48,500
I remember the past two or three years okay, but anything before that is a complete blur.

300
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:49,100
Crazy.

301
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:50,840
So you don't remember Mom either?

302
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:51,680
No.

303
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:53,740
No, I'm afraid I don't.

304
00:14:53,980 --> 00:14:57,460
Then how do you know for sure that you and Shido are actually related to each other?

305
00:14:57,460 --> 00:15:01,500
Is that me?

306
00:15:02,140 --> 00:15:03,840
A lot of little boys look alike.

307
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:06,100
No, this is definitely Shido.

308
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:09,080
Like I said, my memory's pretty fuzzy.

309
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:12,380
But I do remember my older brother going off somewhere.

310
00:15:13,100 --> 00:15:14,360
I was so devastated.

311
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:17,320
But more than that, I spent every day worrying about him.

312
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:18,920
That's why I'm so happy.

313
00:15:19,540 --> 00:15:21,380
And now you're sitting right in front of me.

314
00:15:21,520 --> 00:15:22,460
I can't explain.

315
00:15:22,780 --> 00:15:23,660
I'm ecstatic.

316
00:15:24,820 --> 00:15:25,300
Mana!

317
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,260
I love you, brother!

318
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:29,500
Get away from her!

319
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:32,720
What do you think you're doing?

320
00:15:32,920 --> 00:15:34,120
What the hell was that for?

321
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:35,720
Shido is my family.

322
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:39,240
I'm not going to let you or anyone else take him away from me.

323
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:41,220
I wasn't planning on doing that.

324
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:42,160
You weren't?

325
00:15:42,940 --> 00:15:45,400
I just haven't gotten to see him in such a long time.

326
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:46,900
I'm relieved he's doing well.

327
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:50,820
And even now, he's still got a cute little sister looking after him.

328
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:52,280
Oh, thank you.

329
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:54,740
You should have opened your mouth before I kicked him.

330
00:15:54,740 --> 00:15:58,420
Besides, at the end of the day, there's no beating the real sister.

331
00:15:59,620 --> 00:16:00,080
Funny.

332
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:01,820
You are joking, right?

333
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:02,260
Nope.

334
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:03,800
I'm only stating facts.

335
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,180
There's no bond stronger than blood that I know of.

336
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:09,580
I think you mean better as a neighbor who is near than a sister far away.

337
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:10,540
Hmm?

338
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:11,660
No, no.

339
00:16:12,140 --> 00:16:14,300
An adopted sister's practically a stranger.

340
00:16:14,820 --> 00:16:18,080
A real sister will always be closer because she shares the same blood.

341
00:16:18,540 --> 00:16:21,000
What's the point of emphasizing the blood part?

342
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:22,800
Adopted or real?

343
00:16:23,060 --> 00:16:24,380
What does all of this mean?

344
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:25,600
Do you have any idea?

345
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:26,820
Wake up, you two!

346
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:31,420
Everyone knows a sister can drive a man wild like Forbidden Fruit, sweet, but just the

347
00:16:31,420 --> 00:16:32,520
right amount of tangy.

348
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:32,920
Really?

349
00:16:33,180 --> 00:16:35,020
Then sisters drive me wild, too.

350
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:36,640
I want some Forbidden Fruit.

351
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:38,640
Quit putting ideas in Atoka's head.

352
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:40,260
Just how much is your blood worth?

353
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:41,180
Big whoop.

354
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:43,040
It's not like a real sister could marry him.

355
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:43,500
Huh?

356
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:43,820
Uh.

357
00:16:44,280 --> 00:16:44,460
Uh.

358
00:16:44,460 --> 00:16:44,520
Uh.

359
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:47,520
Um, never mind.

360
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:49,460
Point is, his only sister is me.

361
00:16:49,540 --> 00:16:50,980
I don't think you make a very good one.

362
00:16:51,100 --> 00:16:52,960
You're not as strong as his real little sister.

363
00:16:53,060 --> 00:16:55,620
That has nothing to do with being a sister, you jerk face.

364
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:57,640
Hey, girls, let's try to stay calm.

365
00:16:57,840 --> 00:17:02,540
Shito, which do you like more, an actual blood sister or a stupid adopted sister?

366
00:17:02,740 --> 00:17:03,840
Whoa, I'll pass.

367
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:04,240
Yeah.

368
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:06,240
I mean, talk about awkward, right?

369
00:17:06,540 --> 00:17:08,180
Um, do you live by yourself nowadays?

370
00:17:08,520 --> 00:17:08,700
Uh.

371
00:17:09,180 --> 00:17:12,840
If someone out there's taking care of you, then I ought to at least meet them and tell them

372
00:17:12,840 --> 00:17:13,220
thanks.

373
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:14,940
That's not a good idea.

374
00:17:15,320 --> 00:17:15,840
How come?

375
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:17,860
Is there something wrong with where you're living or what?

376
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:19,080
I wouldn't say that.

377
00:17:19,440 --> 00:17:23,240
See, the thing is, it's kind of a special dorm for people I sort of work with.

378
00:17:23,300 --> 00:17:24,160
Wait, work with?

379
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:25,960
Hold on, you already have a job?

380
00:17:26,100 --> 00:17:29,180
Oh, um, I can't really explain it all that well.

381
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:33,320
See you guys later.

382
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:37,500
What was that all about?

383
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:41,940
And Shimada?

384
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:42,520
Here.

385
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:43,940
And Suzuki?

386
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:44,720
Here.

387
00:17:45,220 --> 00:17:46,220
And Tokisaki?

388
00:17:46,860 --> 00:17:48,260
Is Tokisaki here?

389
00:17:49,180 --> 00:17:49,700
Tokisaki?

390
00:17:50,080 --> 00:17:50,900
She's gone?

391
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:51,660
Wow.

392
00:17:51,980 --> 00:17:53,000
I can't believe it.

393
00:17:53,140 --> 00:17:54,980
Just her second day and she's already late.

394
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:55,700
She's not here.

395
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:59,640
Kurumi Tokisaki will no longer be attending this school.

396
00:17:59,640 --> 00:18:03,640
I told her to contact us in case something like this ever came up.

397
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:04,660
Kids these days.

398
00:18:04,840 --> 00:18:05,420
I'm here.

399
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:06,160
Huh?

400
00:18:08,340 --> 00:18:10,400
Miss Tokisaki, you're very late.

401
00:18:10,780 --> 00:18:12,400
Yeah, sorry about that, Teach.

402
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:16,460
I felt a little queasy on my way here, so I decided to take a quick nap.

403
00:18:16,460 --> 00:18:19,180
Oh, do you feel better now?

404
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:20,280
That's good.

405
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:22,220
Another minute and she'd have been marked absent.

406
00:18:23,180 --> 00:18:24,540
Are you okay, Origami?

407
00:18:28,120 --> 00:18:30,840
Come to the physics preparation room during lunch.

408
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:32,560
There's something I want to show you.

409
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:39,840
So, what's up?

410
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:40,920
Why'd you call me in?

411
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:45,400
There's a sequel?

412
00:18:45,940 --> 00:18:46,280
Oops.

413
00:18:46,640 --> 00:18:47,620
Sorry about that.

414
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:48,520
Wrong window.

415
00:18:49,620 --> 00:18:51,220
This is footage from yesterday.

416
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:52,400
Who's that?

417
00:18:53,180 --> 00:18:54,000
Kurumi and Mana?

418
00:18:55,220 --> 00:18:56,940
Origami and the A.S.T.?

419
00:18:56,940 --> 00:18:57,580
Why?

420
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,500
They wouldn't show up unless there was a spirit around.

421
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:11,280
No way.

422
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:11,320
No way.

423
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:38,080
What is this?

424
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:39,580
The facts.

425
00:19:40,340 --> 00:19:43,400
Yesterday, Kurumi Tokisaki was killed by the A.S.T.

426
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:45,620
And Mana was the one who took her out.

427
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:47,960
So you can see, video doesn't lie.

428
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:50,580
Kurumi Tokisaki should be dead.

429
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:51,780
But how?

430
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:52,300
No.

431
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:53,560
It can't be.

432
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:54,600
Kurumi came to class.

433
00:19:54,680 --> 00:19:55,280
She's alive.

434
00:19:55,340 --> 00:19:55,680
I know.

435
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:57,100
Kind of weird, don't you think?

436
00:19:58,300 --> 00:19:59,140
Yes, I do.

437
00:19:59,800 --> 00:20:01,320
I don't have an explanation.

438
00:20:01,320 --> 00:20:03,920
Hello, Origami.

439
00:20:04,380 --> 00:20:05,900
You wanted to see me about something?

440
00:20:06,340 --> 00:20:08,360
Oh, but first, I haven't eaten lunch.

441
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:09,760
Would you like to grab a bite with me?

442
00:20:10,180 --> 00:20:12,100
You were supposed to have died yesterday.

443
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:13,820
I was?

444
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:14,540
Oh, yeah.

445
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:15,880
Yeah, I remember.

446
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:19,560
You were flitting around with Mana when she murdered me, isn't that right?

447
00:20:19,560 --> 00:20:32,300
What a temper on you.

448
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:34,440
Try to calm yourself down.

449
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:37,140
You took real good care of me yesterday.

450
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:39,580
Cleaned it up as if nothing ever happened.

451
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:41,680
Well, guess what?

452
00:20:42,020 --> 00:20:43,920
I'm not dead.

453
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:46,100
What is this?

454
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:48,620
What are you going to do to me?

455
00:20:48,620 --> 00:20:50,040
Oh, you'll see.

456
00:20:50,800 --> 00:20:55,920
You could say I wanted to try out school, and I even admit it has been a fun experience.

457
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:58,260
But no, that's not why I'm here.

458
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:00,320
I'm here for the same reason you are.

459
00:21:00,740 --> 00:21:01,480
It's for Shido.

460
00:21:01,780 --> 00:21:02,780
I think you know him.

461
00:21:03,380 --> 00:21:04,900
You crave him, too, after all.

462
00:21:05,280 --> 00:21:08,260
But unfortunately for you, he means much more to me.

463
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:10,040
So much more.

464
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:16,260
So if you know what's good for you, get out of my way and never talk to Shido again.

465
00:21:16,260 --> 00:21:18,440
He is absolutely a delight.

466
00:21:18,620 --> 00:21:20,740
And he makes me feel amazing.

467
00:21:21,080 --> 00:21:22,440
He also looks delicious.

468
00:21:24,240 --> 00:21:25,960
I yearn for little Shido.

469
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:29,860
I long for that boy.

470
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:32,000
I want him so badly.

471
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:34,720
I want his entire body for myself.

472
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:37,440
I want all the power he has inside.

473
00:21:37,940 --> 00:21:40,500
And I know what it'll take in order to have him.

474
00:21:41,080 --> 00:21:43,920
Before you know it, Shido is going to be mine.

475
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:44,920
I want him so badly.

476
00:21:44,920 --> 00:21:45,920
I want him so badly.

477
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:46,540
I want him so badly.

478
00:21:46,540 --> 00:21:47,540
I want him so badly.

479
00:21:47,540 --> 00:21:48,540
I want him so badly.

480
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:49,200
I want him so badly.

481
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:51,080
I want him so badly.

482
00:21:51,700 --> 00:21:53,400
I want him so Jaun.

483
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:54,500
I want him so badly.

484
00:21:54,500 --> 00:22:24,480
Let's go!

485
00:22:24,500 --> 00:22:54,480
Let's go!

486
00:22:54,500 --> 00:23:24,480
Let's go!

487
00:23:24,500 --> 00:23:54,480
Let's go!

